# CP-2E and absorbed CP-2F — actual macro/hedging and ESG review

Open the actual CP-0, annual/quarterly CP-1, CP-1A, CP-2 synthesis/update, CP-1B,
CP-1D and CP-2D handoffs. Hash consumed inputs and keep periods/definitions exact.
Use the annual FY2024 PDF's actual market-risk, derivatives, input-cost, climate,
environmental and product/operating-risk disclosures. The December quarter is
separate subsequent evidence, never silently blended into the September base.
Execution: current host model with local tools, no provider/API or legacy owner.

Select the Deploy V-derived analytical breadth in the CP-2E skill and its
REF_CP-2E_STEPS and REF_CP-2F_STEPS companions, preserving later source, precision,
missingness and declared-assumption protections. All macro/ESG questions
must be considered. Follow the current six-heading Markdown transport rather
than inherited invocation/frontmatter/role machinery. Retain source revisions.

Macro: source gate; facility-level fixed/floating exposures and currency; swaps,
caps, collars and forwards with dates/strikes/linkage; gross, hedged and unhedged
amounts; rate sensitivity; FX mismatch/natural offsets; commodity/inflation and
pass-through; synthesis; gaps. Separate notional, effective date, economic
protection, accounting hedge status and fair value. Do not apply future hedges
early, sum overlapping notional as protection, or substitute receivables/cash for
debt exposure. Preserve principal versus carrying debt.

Keep the issuer's reported approximately 30 USDm rate sensitivity and 77% fixed-
rate statement attributed. An independent gross linear calculation has a different
basis and does not establish net sensitivity. Do not reverse-engineer a hedge
ratio to force agreement. Reuse applicable pure arithmetic and probe the imported
single-facility/quote/floor limits against actual source inputs; no invented zero
floor, perfect hedge or FX EBITDA share. Conditional illustrations using a
reported sensitivity must state every holding-constant assumption, proxy meaning
and scope; they are neither a forecast nor an independent hedge reconstruction.

ESG/CP-2F: source reliability; issuer-specific environmental/transition exposure;
social/safety/operating exposure; materiality before credit inference; actual
sustainability-linked instrument/KPI/SPT/ratchet terms; refinancing/access link;
credit synthesis and targeted gaps. Read the environmental liability amounts and
estimate uncertainty. A target is not achieved performance, weak disclosure is
not proven greenwashing, and a debt term not reviewed is not a zero ratchet.
Reference CP-1A governance without repeating its scoring.

Use Python for supported sums/sensitivities and independent integer/Fraction
expectations. Keep exact values, units, dates and source quotes/locators. Show
all T2F.1–9 and T2G.1–8 analytical registers under their selected descriptive
meanings. Unknown quantities remain null, not zero. State credible contrary
evidence, causal downside, time-aware monitoring and what would change the view.

Compare output against instructions and issuer evidence before release. Full
coverage requires the applicable evidence, not a registry alias alone. The next
analytical consumer must actually open and use the response and its limitations.
